From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Subject: [PATCH] i_system: I_Quit and I_Error must exit

Without ORIGCODE (undefined in config.h) both returned or spun:

- I_Quit ran the exit functions, which free the video buffer, and
  returned into the game loop. Backspace and Quit Game both go through
  it. On the badge (NOMMU, no memory protection) the stray writes hung
  the kernel until the watchdog reset it.
- I_Error spun at full CPU forever, a black screen until killed, e.g.
  when the zone did not fit ("Unable to allocate 4 MiB of RAM for
  zone"). Exiting lets the start menu retry with a smaller zone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/fbdoom/i_system.c
+++ b/fbdoom/i_system.c
@@ -259,9 +259,13 @@
 
 #if ORIGCODE
     SDL_Quit();
+#endif
 
+    /* Without ORIGCODE this returned into the game loop, which went on
+     * drawing into the video buffer the exit functions just freed. On
+     * NOMMU there is no fault to stop that: it corrupted memory and hung
+     * the badge (Backspace or Quit Game, then the watchdog reset). */
     exit(0);
-#endif
 }
 
 #if !defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__MACOSX__)
@@ -457,13 +461,11 @@
     // abort();
 #if ORIGCODE
     SDL_Quit();
+#endif
 
+    /* Without ORIGCODE this spun forever at full CPU, a black screen
+     * until killed (e.g. "Unable to allocate 4 MiB of RAM for zone"). */
     exit(-1);
-#else
-    while (true)
-    {
-    }
-#endif
 }
 
